<span id="groups-title" class="anchor-alias" aria-hidden="true"></span><span
  id="groups-close-title"
  class="anchor-alias"
  aria-hidden="true"></span>
<section
  class="feature-copy-grid feature-copy-grid--top"
  aria-labelledby="group-behavior-title"
>
  <div>
    <p class="section-kicker">keep work in context</p><h2
      id="group-behavior-title"
    >
      Groups have names, not colors.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Name the task, then keep moving.</h3><p>
        Use <code>/group work</code> to create or join a named group from the active
        tab. A group exists only while it has tabs in it.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Keep the active group close.</h3><p>
        The resting island shows the active group's tabs. Group names and the
        rest of your groups live in the expanded panel, where you can choose
        what to return to.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Drag tabs and groups into order.</h3><p>
        In the expanded Island or in vertical tabs, drag a tab to reorder it within its group, move it into another group, or take it out of its group. Drop a tab on a group&rsquo;s header to add it, even when the group is folded. Drag a header to move the whole group; ⌘1 to ⌘9 on a Mac, or Ctrl+1 to Ctrl+9 on Windows and Linux, follow the new order.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Or move them from the keyboard.</h3><p>
        Focus a tab or a group header and press Option+Shift+Up or Down on a Mac, or Alt+Shift+Up or Down on Windows and Linux. Folded groups are skipped, and pinned tabs stay pinned.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Fold the rest without losing the thread.</h3><p>
        Groups can tuck away in the panel, and the Quick Switcher finds them by
        name when it is time to return.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<aside class="truth-note" aria-labelledby="groups-note-title">
  <p class="section-kicker">fewer things asking for attention</p><h2
    id="groups-note-title"
  >
    A group is a focus tool, not another layer of browser chrome.
  </h2><p>
    Blanc gives the active task a quiet place in the island while keeping the
    rest of your session nearby. Pinned tabs stay with their group, and a plain
    new tab starts ungrouped.
  </p><a
